---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Layerwatch"
  description="How Layerwatch collects, uses, and protects your information."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  effective="August 21, 2026"
>
  <section>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>
      This policy covers <strong class="text-white">layerwatch.dev</strong> and the free tools we publish
      (including the Layerwatch collector, local UI and MCP server once released). It explains what we collect,
      why, and how you can control it. The short version: we collect as little as possible, and we never
      sell your data.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <p>We collect information in two ways:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-white">Early-access requests.</strong> When you submit an early-access form on
        this site, your email address, and any optional note you choose to add about your team or setup,
        are sent to and stored by our form provider, Formspree, so we can follow up about access and
        product updates.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-white">Automatic connection logs.</strong> Like most websites, requests to
        layerwatch.dev pass through our hosting provider, Cloudflare, which logs standard technical data
        (IP address, browser type, request timestamps) for security and performance. We don't run our own
        analytics or tracking scripts on this site, and our fonts are served from our own domain rather
        than a third-party font service.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How we use your information</h2>
    <p>
      We use your email, and any note you send, solely to reach out about early access and material product updates. We do not
      sell, rent, or share your information with third parties for marketing purposes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>We rely on a small number of infrastructure providers to run this site:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong class="text-white">Formspree</strong> — processes early-access form submissions.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-white">Cloudflare</strong> — hosting, CDN, and security.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Each operates under its own privacy policy governing the data it processes on our behalf.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      layerwatch.dev does not set its own tracking or advertising cookies. Cloudflare may set minimal,
      essential cookies required for security and site performance.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Data retention</h2>
    <p>
      We retain your email address, and any note you sent, for as long as you remain on the early-access list. You can request removal at
      any time — see Contact below.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal data at any time by
      contacting us. We will respond within a reasonable timeframe.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Our services are not directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect information from anyone
      under the age of 16.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Our products</h2>
    <p>
      Layerwatch is designed to run on your own machine or inside infrastructure you control. In local
      mode, collected evidence is stored in a local workspace and is not sent to Layerwatch. If you choose to
      use a hosted AI model for analysis, redacted source excerpts are sent to that model provider under your
      configuration. We will publish detailed data-handling documentation with each release.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, we'll update the effective date above and, for material changes, notify the
      early-access list by email.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy or your data? Email
      <a href="mailto:hi@layerwatch.dev">hi@layerwatch.dev</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
